cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Click'n'Translate in research, please cite the software using the
  metadata below and archive the exact release or commit used in your study.
title: "Click'n'Translate"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khalilov
    given-names: Dzhabrail Elnurovich
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-2391-692X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jabrailkhalil/clickntranslate"
url: "https://github.com/jabrailkhalil/clickntranslate"
version: 1.6.0
date-released: 2026-08-16
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Click'n'Translate is a cross-platform desktop application for capturing,
  recognizing, copying, and translating text from graphical user interfaces.
  It provides multiple local OCR backends, online and offline translation
  routes, versioned release artifacts, and testable platform adapters for
  research on screen text and multilingual interface workflows.
keywords:
  - screen text
  - optical character recognition
  - machine translation
  - graphical user interface
  - accessibility
  - research software
